@nsobid-646761F643AFEBB379EDD5E6A5151AF2CEF93DC1

# Metroid Dread 2.1.0 - Full framerate cutscenes

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Runs real-time cutscenes at the same framerate as gameplay, normally 60.
//
// Two things hold cutscenes at 30:
//
// 1. Entering a cinematic calls the "SetFramerate" script binding
//    (sub_71001D73EC), which picks NVN present interval 2 while the cinematic
//    flag is set. This forces interval 1. The flag itself is left alone, so
//    the cinematic camera, letterboxing and cutscene shadow scale still apply.
//
// 2. Cutscenes with a voice/music stream are audio-synced: the main loop
//    takes its frame delta from the stream position (sub_710119A3D0) and skips
//    update and render entirely when that delta is ~0. The stream position is
//    samples consumed / sample rate, which only advances once per audio buffer,
//    so only every other 60 Hz frame gets drawn. This makes the delta come
//    from the real frame timer instead. The engine's own sync still applies on
//    top: the delta is scaled by stream time / cutscene time, and a lag of more
//    than 0.5 s is caught up in one step, so audio and animation stay aligned.
//
// Prerendered .webm videos are not affected.

@enabled
001D742C E003082A   // MOV W0,W8 = interval 1 (was CINC W0,W8,NE = 2 in cinematics)
0119A47C 1F2003D5   // NOP = keep timer delta (was FCSEL S0,S1,S0,GT = audio stream delta)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Metroid Dread 2.1.0 (MercurySteam engine,
// NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was located by
// structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
